    # Portuguese (Brazil). Machine translated, NOT reviewed by a native speaker - see the
    # header of Tlc.Localization.psm1. Safe for what it covers: field labels, buttons and
    # hints. Nothing that reaches a bundle is translated.
    #
    # Product names stay in English on purpose. "Teams admin center", "Teams Rooms" and
    # "PowerShell" are what the controls in those products actually say, so translating them
    # would send an engineer looking for something that does not exist under that name.
    #
    # One word per concept: "log" for log - the ordinary term in Brazilian IT, and the form
    # an engineer will also meet in the English documentation - and "rastreamento" for
    # trace, everywhere.
    #
    # THIS FILE MUST BE SAVED AS UTF-8 WITH A BOM. Without one, Import-PowerShellDataFile on
    # Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads the bytes as the ANSI codepage and every accent becomes
    # mojibake, while PowerShell 7 reads it correctly either way.

